		}
		{
			description: [
				"Here is the first thing I will teach you that matters."
				""
				"The Pure Daisy does not fight, does not harvest, does not produce. It simply insists — quietly, over hours — that the world nearby should be clean. Set it beside dead wood and wait."
				""
				"Do not stand over it. It will not work faster because you are impatient."
			]
			id: "4E443E17B39C4FF1"
			rewards: [{
				id: "245511970DD444B5"
				item: "botania:apothecary_default"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "The first flower"
			tasks: [{
				id: "055C23524F8687B3"
				item: "botania:pure_daisy"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "The Pure Daisy"
			x: 1.5d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Your daisy will give you Dreamwood."
				""
				"I want you to understand why that is strange. In every account you were ever taught, an elf trades *for* Dreamwood — it is the far material, the one that comes through the gate. Here it grows out of dead logs in your own hands."
				""
				"We are on the other side of the gate now. What was exotic is native. What was ordinary is gone. Livingwood — plain, human Livingwood — you will not see again until you can trade for it."
			]
			id: "6C3C69F4EDB35C64"
			rewards: [{
				count: 8
				id: "63F0CA0716C598AB"
				item: "botania:dreamwood"
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Not Livingwood"
			tasks: [{
